From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SpeakerPoint firmware
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0000
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the phantom libstdc++ NEEDED entry via --as-needed

With our build options (no --with-convolution, no --with-apple-alac),
shairport-sync compiles zero C++ object files - apple_alac.cpp and
FFTConvolver/*.cpp are gated behind AM_CONDITIONALs that are false
here. Automake still decides the target's link driver by scanning all
sources textually referenced in *_SOURCES across the whole file,
conditionals or not, so it emits shairport_sync_LINK = $(CXXLINK)
regardless. g++ unconditionally adds -lstdc++, giving the binary a
real (per readelf -d) but entirely unused NEEDED entry, which is what
stops it from being pruned even though nothing calls into it.

--as-needed drops any NEEDED entry a binary doesn't actually
reference a symbol from - the standard fix for exactly this.

--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ noinst_HEADERS =

 bin_PROGRAMS = shairport-sync

+AM_LDFLAGS = -Wl,--as-needed
+
 BUILT_SOURCES =
 noinst_HEADERS =
 CLEANFILES =
